1
00:00:05,989 --> 00:00:09,593
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:13,196 --> 00:00:15,165
Whoever you are, stop it already!

3
00:00:15,332 --> 00:00:17,067
It keeps getting bigger.

4
00:00:17,134 --> 00:00:19,369
What're we gonna do, Shin'ichi?!

5
00:00:20,871 --> 00:00:23,273
Ala? Let's go.

6
00:00:30,881 --> 00:00:32,783
Hey... what's this date?

7
00:00:32,883 --> 00:00:35,485
Probably... that case.

8
00:00:39,056 --> 00:00:40,757
"Ramen Revolutionary, Noguchi Hyogoro"

9
00:00:48,065 --> 00:00:48,865
"Naguchi Family Eldest Daughter
Noguchi Yuri"

10
00:00:48,932 --> 00:00:50,167
What are you doing here?!

11
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:52,335
The mistress's child shouldn't be butting in!

12
00:00:52,903 --> 00:00:53,603
Listen!

13
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:56,073
"Noguchi Family 2nd Daughter - Noguchi Miki"
I may be his mistress's child...

14
00:00:56,173 --> 00:00:58,075
...but I'm the one Father loved most!

15
00:00:58,909 --> 00:01:02,045
You're calling him Father?!
You're just a good-for-nothing!

16
00:01:02,512 --> 00:01:04,214
At any rate, your only objective is his money!

17
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:07,084
Huh?! You bitch pig!
Get out right now!

18
00:01:07,117 --> 00:01:09,086
*"Noguchi Family Butler - Kamoshita Ryosuke"
Stop this! Yuri-ojyosama!

19
00:01:09,219 --> 00:01:11,088
"Suzuki Sonoko"
Miki-san, calm down!

20
00:01:11,388 --> 00:01:12,756
Let go!

21
00:01:12,856 --> 00:01:14,691
Thank you for waiting.

22
00:01:14,758 --> 00:01:17,394
What was Sonoko doing at
the funeral of the Ramen King?

23
00:01:17,561 --> 00:01:21,865
Her Dad and him were close friends,
and their families socialized.

24
00:01:21,965 --> 00:01:25,102
Ah... Rich people are all connected
to one another.

25
00:01:25,435 --> 00:01:27,537
Ah, here's my chance.
If you don't want it, I'll take it.

26
00:01:27,604 --> 00:01:28,738
Eh... Ah?!

27
00:01:29,439 --> 00:01:32,642
You're terrible!
I was saving that for last.

28
00:01:32,742 --> 00:01:33,610
Revenge!

29
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:36,913
Whaa, you...
I was saving that for last!

30
00:01:37,214 --> 00:01:38,815
Geez...

31
00:01:39,549 --> 00:01:40,650
Ah!

32
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:42,185
"Incoming call
Suzuki Sonoko's Home"

33
00:01:42,252 --> 00:01:43,987
It's from Sonoko.

34
00:01:46,123 --> 00:01:47,657
Hello...

35
00:01:48,258 --> 00:01:50,760
No way?! Sonoko has?!

36
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:54,064
What's the matter with Sonoko?

37
00:01:55,132 --> 00:01:56,566
She's been kidnapped!

38
00:01:56,666 --> 00:01:58,135
Eh?

39
00:02:11,581 --> 00:02:13,617
"Hyogoro Ramen Headquarters"

40
00:02:15,085 --> 00:02:18,321
"Legendary Meat Soup!"

41
00:02:19,089 --> 00:02:21,491
What do you mean by
Sonoko's been kidnapped?

42
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,460
I got a phone call at the crematorium...

43
00:02:23,527 --> 00:02:27,063
I don't know if it was a man or a woman.
The voice had been processed.

44
00:02:27,364 --> 00:02:29,733
"I've kidnapped your older sister,
Noguchi Yuri."

45
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:34,070
"If you want her returned to you,
have 10 billion in diamonds prepared."

46
00:02:34,604 --> 00:02:35,972
Diamonds...?

47
00:02:36,273 --> 00:02:40,243
"If you don't abide by these demands,
your sister will lose her life."

48
00:02:40,343 --> 00:02:43,480
"We don't have just your sister."

49
00:02:43,647 --> 00:02:45,482
"Wait... what do you mean?!"

50
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:49,186
Then the phone got cut off.

51
00:02:50,387 --> 00:02:51,621
After the funeral...

52
00:02:51,688 --> 00:02:56,593
...both my sister and Sonoko-chan seem to have
left the temple and been together since then.

53
00:02:58,161 --> 00:03:03,133
So it looks as if Sonoko-chan
was kidnapped as well.

54
00:03:03,466 --> 00:03:05,135
Sonoko...

55
00:03:12,075 --> 00:03:14,144
Sonoko, pick up!

56
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,494
It's no good... It's been turned off.

57
00:03:32,762 --> 00:03:35,265
Yuri-san's car was found in
the temple's parking lot.

58
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:36,066
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Takagi Wataru"

59
00:03:36,099 --> 00:03:41,471
So your sister and Sonoko-san were probably
kidnapped together at the temple.

60
00:03:41,571 --> 00:03:44,541
Has there been a ransom demand
made to Sonoko's family?

61
00:03:44,641 --> 00:03:45,842
Not at present.

62
00:03:46,509 --> 00:03:49,446
But... that's weird, isn't it?

63
00:03:49,746 --> 00:03:53,850
Because even Sonoko's family
is incredibly rich.

64
00:03:54,351 --> 00:03:56,586
Is it that the criminal doesn't know that...

65
00:03:56,653 --> 00:04:00,657
...and their only target is to take money
from the Noguchi family...?

66
00:04:43,166 --> 00:04:44,467
Yuri?

67
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:45,802
Yuri?

68
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,604
Yuri?!

69
00:04:47,737 --> 00:04:49,606
Yuri!

70
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:54,678
Miki-ojyosama.

71
00:04:54,778 --> 00:04:56,112
I have brought the diamonds.

72
00:04:56,179 --> 00:04:58,248
- Thank you. Put them there.
- Yes.

73
00:04:58,615 --> 00:05:03,586
This is the first time I've seen
so many diamonds.

74
00:05:03,687 --> 00:05:04,387
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Sato Miwako"

75
00:05:04,454 --> 00:05:07,624
It's because the Ramen King was
known for his diamond collection, huh?

76
00:05:08,291 --> 00:05:09,926
Ah... you dropped them.

77
00:05:10,026 --> 00:05:12,128
This is terrible, terrible...

78
00:05:12,796 --> 00:05:15,732
Thanks to my sister, these'll be squandered.

79
00:05:15,832 --> 00:05:18,468
You were having a big fight with her on TV...

80
00:05:18,535 --> 00:05:20,737
...but truth is,
you do care for your sister, don't you?

81
00:05:20,870 --> 00:05:22,272
You're wrong.

82
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:26,176
If we're stingy with the ransom money
and my sister is killed...

83
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:29,846
...that would damage
the Noguchi family name, wouldn't it?

84
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,916
Is that right...

85
00:05:33,516 --> 00:05:35,919
It would be best to put
the diamonds all in one place.

86
00:05:35,952 --> 00:05:38,455
Kamoshita.
Bring me my attache case.

87
00:05:38,521 --> 00:05:39,756
Certainly.

88
00:05:51,201 --> 00:05:52,268
It's OK.

89
00:05:52,335 --> 00:05:53,870
If you would please.

90
00:05:57,674 --> 00:05:58,708
Hello?

91
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,710
"Are the diamonds ready?"

92
00:06:00,844 --> 00:06:02,712
Yes, they're prepared.

93
00:06:02,812 --> 00:06:05,815
Please let me hear Yuri-oneesama's voice.

94
00:06:05,882 --> 00:06:10,186
"It would be better for you to pray for
her safety than hear her voice."

95
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:14,157
"Attach the diamonds to the rooftop
ad-balloon and send it skyward."

96
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:15,492
Skyward?

97
00:06:15,592 --> 00:06:16,860
"At 3 o'clock."

98
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,697
"Once we've checked the contents, we'll notify
you of the whereabouts of the two people."

99
00:06:22,866 --> 00:06:24,200
Please give it to me!

100
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:27,270
How's Sonoko?
Are you with Sonoko?!

101
00:06:27,537 --> 00:06:30,006
Hello?! Hello?!

102
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,175
The trace failed!

103
00:06:35,111 --> 00:06:36,446
Shin'ichi...

104
00:06:43,119 --> 00:06:44,454
Give it to me!

105
00:06:52,729 --> 00:06:55,665
There's only 10 minutes left.
Let's hurry.

106
00:07:03,106 --> 00:07:06,843
How are they going to check
the contents from the sky?

107
00:07:06,910 --> 00:07:09,212
Fool.
They're going to check it now.

108
00:07:09,245 --> 00:07:10,713
Kyaa!

109
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:13,583
Are you okay?

110
00:07:13,817 --> 00:07:15,885
I just fell down for a moment.

111
00:07:20,423 --> 00:07:22,625
I'll carry that.

112
00:07:22,826 --> 00:07:23,960
Yes.

113
00:07:25,161 --> 00:07:27,096
If you would please.

114
00:07:27,263 --> 00:07:31,067
Just the sort of feel you'd expect from
10 billion yen worth of diamonds.

115
00:07:31,234 --> 00:07:32,402
Let's go.

116
00:07:38,475 --> 00:07:40,510
Everything's fine over here.

117
00:07:41,177 --> 00:07:42,645
Same here.

118
00:07:54,123 --> 00:07:57,494
How will the criminal snatch away
the diamonds from such a place?

119
00:07:57,627 --> 00:08:00,096
Will a helicopter come?

120
00:08:00,129 --> 00:08:01,297
Eh?!

121
00:08:40,236 --> 00:08:41,538
It's 3.

122
00:08:47,577 --> 00:08:49,746
No one's coming to get it.

123
00:08:49,879 --> 00:08:51,514
Should we bring it down?

124
00:08:52,248 --> 00:08:54,484
Let's wait a little longer.

125
00:08:55,251 --> 00:08:57,186
We'll wait a little longer.

126
00:09:13,536 --> 00:09:16,172
I wonder why the criminal isn't appearing?

127
00:09:16,306 --> 00:09:18,875
Did they notice the police activity?

128
00:09:19,175 --> 00:09:22,745
We were taking the latest precautions,
so that can't be so.

129
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:26,482
It's been an hour now...

130
00:09:32,689 --> 00:09:33,957
Hello?

131
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:35,959
"We've got the diamonds."

132
00:09:36,192 --> 00:09:37,427
What's that?!

133
00:09:37,527 --> 00:09:38,895
Was that the criminal?

134
00:09:39,729 --> 00:09:42,799
They said, "We've got the diamonds."

135
00:09:42,865 --> 00:09:44,601
Bring down the balloon!

136
00:10:17,567 --> 00:10:20,336
The diamonds... are gone!

137
00:10:23,206 --> 00:10:25,274
The diamonds disappeared?!

138
00:10:25,441 --> 00:10:26,943
Miki-ojyosama...

139
00:10:32,081 --> 00:10:34,884
"As promised, the hostages will be returned."

140
00:10:35,084 --> 00:10:37,920
"Go to the bench at Beika Central Park."

141
00:10:38,021 --> 00:10:39,622
Beika Central Park?

142
00:10:39,756 --> 00:10:41,157
Why...?

143
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:47,630
"Beika Central Park"

144
00:10:51,367 --> 00:10:54,070
It said Beika Central Park bench,
but which bench?!

145
00:10:54,137 --> 00:10:56,706
At any rate, let's split up and look for it.

146
00:10:57,206 --> 00:10:59,275
- Look at that one, please.
- Yes! Certainly!

147
00:10:59,375 --> 00:11:00,777
I'm sorry, may I look here?

148
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:03,413
Excuse us a moment!

149
00:11:03,479 --> 00:11:04,814
I'm sorry.

150
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,784
- Ran-chan, over there, please.
- Ah, yes!

151
00:11:08,518 --> 00:11:10,853
Excuse me! Excuse me a moment...
I'm sorry.

152
00:11:14,857 --> 00:11:15,992
Damn!

153
00:11:16,059 --> 00:11:17,593
Where is it?

154
00:11:28,504 --> 00:11:30,273
"Go to the underground depot."

155
00:11:30,339 --> 00:11:31,741
Underground depot?

156
00:11:32,008 --> 00:11:34,444
There is an underground depot
at the headquarters.

157
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,782
It's no good! It's locked!

158
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:42,385
Sonoko!
Sonoko, are you in there?!

159
00:11:42,485 --> 00:11:43,886
Here is the master key.

160
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,488
Ah, thank you.

161
00:11:48,825 --> 00:11:49,592
Sonoko!

162
00:11:49,659 --> 00:11:50,993
Sonoko!

163
00:11:53,596 --> 00:11:55,598
- Sonoko!
- Sonoko!

164
00:11:55,698 --> 00:11:57,433
Sonoko, are you okay?

165
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,135
Where is Yuri-ojyosama?

166
00:12:00,937 --> 00:12:03,139
Yuri-sama... Ojyosama!

167
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,775
Are you okay?

168
00:12:09,512 --> 00:12:10,513
Kudo-kun...

169
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:12,115
Are you okay?

170
00:12:12,281 --> 00:12:13,616
Thank goodness.

171
00:12:14,617 --> 00:12:17,587
Ojyosama! Yuri-ojyosama!

172
00:12:19,088 --> 00:12:20,389
Kamoshita...

173
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:21,858
Are you injured?

174
00:12:21,958 --> 00:12:24,527
I'll remove the ropes from your feet now.

175
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:25,795
Thank you.

176
00:12:26,028 --> 00:12:27,396
Are you okay?

177
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:30,066
Yes. Yes, I'm fine.

178
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:31,267
This is bad!

179
00:12:32,101 --> 00:12:34,170
Miki-san, on the roof!

180
00:12:44,647 --> 00:12:46,315
She's dead...

181
00:12:55,258 --> 00:12:56,459
Miki...

182
00:12:58,094 --> 00:12:59,862
Yuri-oneesan...

183
00:13:00,263 --> 00:13:02,398
Why has Miki-san...

184
00:13:02,498 --> 00:13:05,835
Right after we went to
Beika Central Park, Miki-san was...

185
00:13:05,935 --> 00:13:09,205
It was the act of the kidnapper
who was lurking somewhere, wasn't it?

186
00:13:10,506 --> 00:13:11,908
"This is strange..."

187
00:13:12,642 --> 00:13:14,944
"The criminal got the diamonds..."

188
00:13:15,511 --> 00:13:18,314
"...so why was it necessary for them
to kill Miki-san?"

189
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:27,957
Well then, please tell us what happened
when you were kidnapped.

190
00:13:28,357 --> 00:13:29,692
Yes...

191
00:13:30,326 --> 00:13:35,531
I was waiting for Yuri-oneesan, who said
she'd forgotten something at the temple.

192
00:13:36,365 --> 00:13:41,437
But since she didn't return at all,
I went back...

193
00:13:42,638 --> 00:13:44,507
"Yuri-oneesan?"

194
00:13:45,541 --> 00:13:47,076
"Kyaa!"

195
00:13:49,412 --> 00:13:51,180
"Yuri-oneesan?"

196
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,085
"Yuri-oneesan!"

197
00:13:57,286 --> 00:14:01,057
By that time, I was already unconscious.

198
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:05,528
I had been made to breathe in
some drug from a handkerchief, too...

199
00:14:05,962 --> 00:14:07,930
Is that right...

200
00:14:08,231 --> 00:14:12,268
I'm sorry.
For getting Sonoko-chan involved in this.

201
00:14:12,501 --> 00:14:13,903
No...

202
00:14:14,370 --> 00:14:18,975
Then, did either of you
get a look at the criminal?

203
00:14:19,876 --> 00:14:24,146
I didn't get the chance to see
anything but their back.

204
00:14:24,981 --> 00:14:27,516
When I came to, I was in that room.

205
00:14:28,853 --> 00:14:31,950
Right before my eyes...
Yuri-oneesan had been tied up as well.

206
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,423
Yes.

207
00:14:34,757 --> 00:14:37,126
Then the lights suddenly went out and...

208
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:39,128
The lights?

209
00:14:39,829 --> 00:14:41,097
Yes...

210
00:14:43,833 --> 00:14:47,503
When they came on again,
Oneesan had fallen over.

211
00:14:47,737 --> 00:14:52,375
I think someone had come in
and made me breathe in the drug again.

212
00:14:52,541 --> 00:14:57,680
And from then until Kamoshita woke me up,
I don't remember anything...

213
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:00,917
Sonoko.

214
00:15:00,983 --> 00:15:03,819
Did the light only go out that once?

215
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:05,254
No.

216
00:15:05,521 --> 00:15:07,223
There was one other time...

217
00:15:09,525 --> 00:15:13,329
Just a little before you guys
came to save me...

218
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:15,298
...they went out again.

219
00:15:16,799 --> 00:15:18,634
I thought so.

220
00:15:18,701 --> 00:15:19,936
Eh?

221
00:15:20,469 --> 00:15:21,938
I've seen it.

222
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:26,475
The one and only truth.

223
00:15:34,583 --> 00:15:38,287
It's impossible for 10 billion in diamonds
to just disappear from the sky.

224
00:15:38,421 --> 00:15:41,157
What's more likely is that before
they were even put up in the sky...

225
00:15:41,257 --> 00:15:43,025
...they had already been substituted.

226
00:15:43,125 --> 00:15:44,593
Substituted?!

227
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:48,631
When? By whom? Where?

228
00:15:48,698 --> 00:15:52,568
Weren't we with the attache case
all the way up to the roof?

229
00:15:53,169 --> 00:15:56,639
Everyone, please line up in turn
the way we were then.

230
00:15:56,839 --> 00:15:58,441
I will stand in for Miki-san...

231
00:15:58,507 --> 00:16:01,243
...and Detective Takagi and Sonoko
and Yuri-san, you stay with Ran.

232
00:16:01,344 --> 00:16:02,578
If you would please.

233
00:16:06,916 --> 00:16:08,884
Well then, let's run.

234
00:16:08,951 --> 00:16:10,653
And, start!

235
00:16:16,192 --> 00:16:17,326
Stop!

236
00:16:19,695 --> 00:16:22,531
Detective Sato, can you see me from there?

237
00:16:23,666 --> 00:16:25,134
I can't.

238
00:16:25,601 --> 00:16:27,703
Ran, how about you?

239
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:29,305
I can't see you!

240
00:16:31,374 --> 00:16:36,045
It was just for a moment,
but Miki-san had entered a blind spot here.

241
00:16:36,479 --> 00:16:40,483
If there was a chance for
a substitution, this would be it.

242
00:16:49,658 --> 00:16:50,626
This is it.

243
00:16:50,693 --> 00:16:52,461
Huh? Where?

244
00:16:52,528 --> 00:16:54,030
Miki-san...

245
00:16:55,564 --> 00:16:57,066
...used this.

246
00:16:57,466 --> 00:16:58,768
Ready?

247
00:16:58,834 --> 00:17:02,438
Beforehand, she had put a fake case in here.

248
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:08,944
And then, when she put the real case in...

249
00:17:12,782 --> 00:17:14,483
Shin'ichi...

250
00:17:14,717 --> 00:17:17,853
...are you saying Miki-san
substituted the attache case?

251
00:17:17,987 --> 00:17:19,055
Yeah.

252
00:17:21,590 --> 00:17:26,128
At that time, Miki-san pretended to fall down
here after substituting the attache case.

253
00:17:26,162 --> 00:17:27,663
"Kyaa!"

254
00:17:28,364 --> 00:17:29,732
"Ah, are you okay?"

255
00:17:29,832 --> 00:17:30,733
Wait!

256
00:17:30,766 --> 00:17:34,036
But then the case I was carrying that time...

257
00:17:34,370 --> 00:17:36,539
"I'll carry that."

258
00:17:36,605 --> 00:17:37,740
"Yes."

259
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,076
"If you would please."

260
00:17:40,743 --> 00:17:44,013
"Just the sort of feel you'd expect from
10 billion yen worth of diamonds."

261
00:17:44,046 --> 00:17:47,616
If it had been
replaced with that empty case...

262
00:17:47,683 --> 00:17:49,685
...it should have felt lighter.

263
00:17:50,286 --> 00:17:54,890
Something that was the same weight as
the 10 billion in diamonds was put in here.

264
00:17:55,091 --> 00:17:58,561
What's more, it was something
that would disappear over time.

265
00:17:58,661 --> 00:18:00,563
Something that would disappear?

266
00:18:01,831 --> 00:18:04,834
Most likely... dry ice.

267
00:18:04,967 --> 00:18:07,369
Please recall what happened on the roof.

268
00:18:07,636 --> 00:18:09,371
"Should we bring it down?"

269
00:18:10,106 --> 00:18:12,041
"Let's wait a little longer."

270
00:18:14,276 --> 00:18:20,216
Miki-san wanted to stop then because the dry ice in
the substituted case hadn't finished evaporating yet.

271
00:18:20,749 --> 00:18:24,120
But, why would Miki do such a thing?

272
00:18:24,487 --> 00:18:26,088
Because she was the criminal.

273
00:18:26,255 --> 00:18:27,823
The criminal?!

274
00:18:28,424 --> 00:18:31,794
This kidnapping was Miki-san's little play.

275
00:18:31,961 --> 00:18:36,665
However, Miki-san was then
killed by the other criminal.

276
00:18:39,401 --> 00:18:41,170
You're saying she had an accomplice?!

277
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,304
If true...

278
00:18:42,438 --> 00:18:46,642
...then shouldn't the attache case with
the 10 billion in diamonds still be in here?

279
00:18:46,842 --> 00:18:47,743
No.

280
00:18:47,810 --> 00:18:50,880
The diamonds have already been collected
by the accomplice.

281
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,949
The one who could have done that...

282
00:18:54,683 --> 00:18:55,784
There's just one person.

283
00:18:55,851 --> 00:18:57,920
Who would that be?

284
00:18:58,988 --> 00:19:00,890
Let's go to the underground depot.

285
00:19:06,095 --> 00:19:10,065
Is there a clue here
that'll lead to the criminal?

286
00:19:10,366 --> 00:19:11,567
Yeah.

287
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:14,937
You've made a lot of insinuations.

288
00:19:15,204 --> 00:19:17,139
You should tell me clearly.

289
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:19,341
Who is the criminal?

290
00:19:19,742 --> 00:19:21,343
The criminal is...

291
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:23,479
You.

292
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:27,016
Noguchi Yuri-san.

293
00:19:28,551 --> 00:19:29,952
Me?

294
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:34,657
It was because you two didn't want anyone to
realize you would be complicit together in it...

295
00:19:34,857 --> 00:19:38,861
...that you deliberately staged a
violent quarrel at that funeral, wasn't it?

296
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:44,033
What do you think you're suggesting?
That's absurd.

297
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:47,002
I was confined down here the entire time.

298
00:19:47,169 --> 00:19:49,305
Sonoko-chan is my witness.

299
00:19:49,638 --> 00:19:51,440
Right, Sonoko-chan?

300
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,142
Yes...

301
00:19:54,210 --> 00:19:59,615
How are you saying I could have
taken away the diamonds and killed Miki?

302
00:20:01,951 --> 00:20:05,487
There was another substitution
made in this room, too.

303
00:20:05,688 --> 00:20:07,056
Substitution?

304
00:20:07,523 --> 00:20:11,293
You used Sonoko in order to
create an alibi for yourself.

305
00:20:12,428 --> 00:20:13,963
What do you mean?

306
00:20:14,296 --> 00:20:16,065
I don't understand what you mean.

307
00:20:16,165 --> 00:20:19,501
What Sonoko saw wasn't Yuri-san.

308
00:20:22,071 --> 00:20:23,405
It was a mannequin.

309
00:20:23,505 --> 00:20:24,807
A mannequin?

310
00:20:26,208 --> 00:20:28,911
The lights in this room went out twice.

311
00:20:29,111 --> 00:20:32,881
The first time was so that Yuri-san
could substitute in a mannequin.

312
00:20:47,930 --> 00:20:50,232
That way, while we were up on the roof...

313
00:20:50,299 --> 00:20:55,638
...Yuri-san could sneak out of this room
and collect the attache case with the diamonds.

314
00:20:59,775 --> 00:21:01,110
At that point...

315
00:21:01,210 --> 00:21:05,714
...yours and Miki-san's plans for the
make-believe kidnapping were complete...

316
00:21:05,881 --> 00:21:07,216
Or were supposed to be.

317
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:10,619
However, you headed for the roof instead.

318
00:21:35,844 --> 00:21:38,480
"Why have you come here?"

319
00:21:38,614 --> 00:21:41,050
"Moreover, what was that about
Beika Central Park?"

320
00:21:41,183 --> 00:21:43,452
"That's different from what we had planned."

321
00:21:45,587 --> 00:21:48,257
"The real plan starts here."

322
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,391
"Eh?"

323
00:21:49,625 --> 00:21:54,296
"Killing you... will complete the first plan."

324
00:22:17,853 --> 00:22:19,955
And when the light went out the second time...

325
00:22:20,022 --> 00:22:23,792
...this time it was so the mannequin
could be substituted out for Yuri-san.

326
00:22:25,494 --> 00:22:30,032
You had us set off for Beika Central Park
so you could make the time you needed...

327
00:22:30,499 --> 00:22:32,067
...to return to this room.

328
00:22:32,201 --> 00:22:33,235
"Sonoko!"

329
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:35,838
"Sonoko! Answer me!"

330
00:22:35,971 --> 00:22:38,741
The light was operated by remote control.

331
00:22:42,878 --> 00:22:44,246
Kudo-san...

332
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:48,717
Everything you've said are fabrications.

333
00:22:49,118 --> 00:22:52,855
And even if I did,
what evidence do you have?

334
00:22:53,756 --> 00:22:56,792
Kamoshita-san is holding the evidence.

335
00:22:57,226 --> 00:22:58,794
Kamoshita is?

336
00:22:59,862 --> 00:23:02,798
Kamoshita-san is holding the evidence.

337
00:23:03,232 --> 00:23:04,600
Kamoshita is?

338
00:23:05,167 --> 00:23:06,268
Kamoshita-san...

339
00:23:06,368 --> 00:23:11,840
...please show us what you picked up in this room
at the time we rescued Sonoko and Yuri-san.

340
00:23:13,108 --> 00:23:14,443
"Are you okay?"

341
00:23:14,910 --> 00:23:16,078
"Yes..."

342
00:23:16,178 --> 00:23:17,946
"You're not injured?"

343
00:23:18,213 --> 00:23:19,782
"I'm fine..."

344
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:26,422
I am very sorry.

345
00:23:26,555 --> 00:23:29,324
I just wished for you two sisters...

346
00:23:29,725 --> 00:23:32,795
I wanted to protect the Noguchi family
with all my heart...

347
00:23:41,336 --> 00:23:45,474
That was from when you killed
Miki-san on the roof, wasn't it?

348
00:23:45,741 --> 00:23:51,313
I think it most likely got into your pants hem
while you were killing her.

349
00:23:59,121 --> 00:24:02,724
And then it fell out again in this room.

350
00:24:06,929 --> 00:24:10,799
Just like the great detective
you're rumored to be.

351
00:24:10,933 --> 00:24:12,401
That's right...

352
00:24:14,236 --> 00:24:16,805
I'm the one who killed her.

353
00:24:21,243 --> 00:24:26,715
But, the one who created that
make-believe kidnapping plan was Miki.

354
00:24:27,950 --> 00:24:34,423
Rather than having our father's
large bequests be hit with inheritance taxes...

355
00:24:34,590 --> 00:24:38,360
...it was she who suggested
we make up a kidnapping...

356
00:24:38,494 --> 00:24:42,764
...with a fictional criminal who would steal
the 10 billion in diamonds.

357
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:50,305
Miki, from the time we were children...

358
00:24:51,273 --> 00:24:53,175
...could come up with cunning schemes like that.

359
00:24:53,509 --> 00:24:56,345
Father loved that in her so much.

360
00:24:56,945 --> 00:25:00,916
That's why Father felt Miki
was the only one he adored.

361
00:25:01,483 --> 00:25:06,088
In his will after all, he was giving her,
his mistress's child, far more than me!

362
00:25:10,225 --> 00:25:11,927
So frustrating...

363
00:25:12,895 --> 00:25:14,263
It was frustrating...

364
00:25:14,463 --> 00:25:16,732
Frustrating, frustrating...

365
00:25:17,032 --> 00:25:20,536
I was always thinking,
"Someday I'll look back in triumph over Miki."

366
00:25:24,506 --> 00:25:26,108
With this...

367
00:25:26,308 --> 00:25:30,078
...I could prove I was
even more cunning than she was.

368
00:25:30,646 --> 00:25:32,648
Even from Heaven...

369
00:25:32,848 --> 00:25:36,685
...I think Father would admit to that as well.

370
00:25:40,756 --> 00:25:44,660
It was just by accident that pearl
got caught in your pants.

371
00:25:44,726 --> 00:25:46,428
But, that accident...

372
00:25:46,762 --> 00:25:49,264
...may have been caused by
your Father in Heaven...

373
00:25:49,464 --> 00:25:52,467
...in order to make you compensate
for your crimes.

374
00:25:52,668 --> 00:25:53,869
You're wrong!

375
00:25:53,936 --> 00:25:56,004
It wasn't an accident!

376
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:59,575
Miki... Miki did it.

377
00:26:16,124 --> 00:26:17,359
She...

378
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:21,897
Right to the very end,
she was a cunning girl.

379
00:27:25,227 --> 00:27:26,695
"Diamond"

380
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,365
"Diamond"

381
00:27:33,602 --> 00:27:35,003
Shin'ichi?

382
00:27:35,604 --> 00:27:37,506
Nothing's changed...

383
00:28:06,468 --> 00:28:08,036
Somehow...

384
00:28:08,537 --> 00:28:11,306
I have a bad feeling about this already.

385
00:28:11,606 --> 00:28:14,443
It's still far from over.

386
00:28:28,557 --> 00:28:30,659
Nothing's happening.

387
00:28:35,097 --> 00:28:35,964
Kyaa!

388
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:41,069
That was... an electric shock.

389
00:28:54,015 --> 00:28:55,650
An electric current?

390
00:29:06,027 --> 00:29:07,229
Ow!

391
00:29:12,434 --> 00:29:15,604
"The Molester is a murderer?!"

392
00:29:17,172 --> 00:29:21,209
"Mystery of the Artificial Respirator
that Stopped"

393
00:29:22,210 --> 00:29:24,279
"This Drama Is Fictional"

